{"name":"Suede Vest","hex":"#d79043","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"suede","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of soft leather, made from calfskin, with a brushed texture to resemble fabric, often used to make boots, clothing and fashion accessories."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of suede."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suede"},{"term":"vest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment that buttons down the front, worn over a shirt, and often as part of a suit; a waistcoat.","A sleeveless garment, often with a low-cut neck, usually worn under a shirt or blouse."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clothe with, or as with, a vestment, or garment; to dress; to robe; to cover, surround, or encompass closely.","To clothe with authority, power, etc.; to put in possession; to invest; to furnish; to endow; followed by with and the thing conferred."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Suede","blocks":[{"text":"Suede is a type of leather with a fuzzy, napped finish, commonly used for jackets, shoes, fabrics, purses, furniture, and other items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Blue_suede_samba.JPG/330px-Blue_suede_samba.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suede"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/George-Boot_Carson_%28Grenson%29.jpg/500px-George-Boot_Carson_%28Grenson%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/George-Boot_Carson_%28Grenson%29.jpg/500px-George-Boot_Carson_%28Grenson%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Suede boot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeorge-Boot_Carson_(Grenson).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wik